 His moral engagement is also reflected in his poetry about the lives of ordinary people , such as the " Three Officers " and " Three Separations " , which are among his most famous works . The " Three Officers " ( 三吏 sān lì ) are a series of three poems about the three officers who were in charge of the local garrisons in the An Lushan Rebellion . The " Three Separations " ( 三别 sān bié ) are three poems about the separation of a man from his wife and children . These poems are considered to be the most important in the history of Chinese poetry because they are the first to give voice to the lives of ordinary people in a way that is both personal and historical
